# ITINERARY Git Nib — Same Commit (seated `20260728.205029`)

When a send updates `construction/ITINERARY.md` **Git nib**, that update lands **in the same work commit** as the round's work (and session log when possible).

## Refuse

- A follow-up commit whose subject is only `work-in-progress: pin ITINERARY git nib` (or `wip: pin ITINERARY…`).
- Two-commit send pairs (work · then pin) for scroll noise.

## How

1. Stage ITINERARY with the round's finishing-edge / bookmark updates in the **work** commit.  
2. After that signed commit, amend **at most once** so **Git nib** names `git rev-parse --short=10 HEAD`.  
3. **Stop.** A second amend to chase a perfect fixed-point hash is refused — GPG trailers shift the hash, so the card may lag HEAD by one amend. Living HEAD is always `prin scope` / `git rev-parse`.  
4. Never push a pin-only follow-up to close that lag.

## Why

Pin-only commits doubled Surface Season history and hurt `git log` scroll reading. Keaton seated this tidy `20260728.205029`.

